// and American AP for expat, EU-institution, finance-sector, and
// Luxembourgish families across Luxembourg City, Esch-sur-Alzette,
// Differdange, the Nordstad, the Moselle, and the frontalier belt.
//
// LEGAL POSITIONING NOTE — READ BEFORE EDITING. TWO HARD RULES:
// Luxembourg is an AUTHORISATION TIER market (with Hungary and
// Austria), and its framework is ACTIVELY BEING REWRITTEN. Both
// facts must appear wherever the law is described.
// - Obligation scolaire runs from age 4 to 16 for every child
//   resident in Luxembourg, national or foreign, across a minimum
//   of twelve consecutive years. It can be met in public, private,
//   or European schools, in Luxembourg or abroad — or at home under
//   conditions set by law.
// - THE 20 JULY 2023 LAW changed the regime materially: it
//   introduced a requirement of PRIOR MINISTERIAL AUTHORISATION for
//   enseignement à domicile INCLUDING at secondary level (ending a
//   previously freer secondary position), gave the Minister of
//   Education responsibility for controlling compliance with the
//   obligation scolaire, and provided for REINFORCED CONTROL of the
//   knowledge and competences acquired by a home-taught minor.
//   Never describe Luxembourg as a declaration/notification market.
// - THE CRITICAL CONSTRAINT: the reform bill under consideration in
//   2025 frames home education around school programmes organised
//   by (1) Luxembourg public establishments, (2) establishments
//   under the European Schools Convention, and (3) private
//   establishments approved by the Luxembourg State — explicitly
//   opening home education to the full public or private school
//   offer established in Luxembourg, and presented as an asset for
//   international families. The practical consequence we must state
//   honestly: an overseas online curriculum is NOT automatically an
//   authorised programme for satisfying the obligation scolaire.
//   Position Smartious FIRST as supplementary alongside an
//   enrolment (always clean), and treat any full-time home
//   education configuration as something the family agrees with the
//   MENJE. NEVER imply we can carry the obligation scolaire alone.
// - The bill also limits in-person home teaching to children of a
//   single household (to prevent unlicensed group schools) — worth
//   knowing, and a reason we describe our own delivery as online.
// - FLUX: because the framework is mid-reform, every legal section
//   must tell families to confirm current requirements with the
//   MENJE. Say the reform exists; do not predict its final shape.
// - AGE 18 QUESTION: an extension of the obligation scolaire from
//   16 to 18 has been under political discussion since 2022. Its
//   current status must NOT be asserted either way — state that the
//   obligation currently runs to 16, note the long-running proposal,
//   and tell families to confirm. NEVER market a post-16 window in
//   Luxembourg the way we do in Hungary or Greece.
// - Home education is genuinely rare here: on ministry figures a
//   few hundred children across the whole country. Say so.
// MARKET NOTE: Luxembourg is the most multilingual school market in
// Europe — the public fundamental system runs Luxembourgish, German,
// then French, which arriving international families frequently find
// impossible to join mid-stream. Against that: the European Schools
// (Lux I Kirchberg, Lux II Bertrange-Mamer) for EU-institution
// families; fee-paying international schools (ISL, St George's on
// the British IGCSE/A-Level track, Lycée Vauban French, and others);
// and — distinctively — a network of PUBLIC international schools
// created since 2016 (Lycée Michel Lucius, École internationale
// Differdange-Esch, Lënster Lycée, Lycée Edward Steichen Clervaux,
// Mondorf) teaching European or IB-style tracks free of charge but
// CAPACITY-GATED. So the gate here is a mix of fees and places, and
// the wedge is capacity + language + continuity, not cost alone.
// ECONOMY: EU institutions (Court of Justice, EIB, Eurostat,
// Parliament secretariat), the world's second-largest investment
// fund domicile, the Big Four, ArcelorMittal, SES satellites,
// Amazon and PayPal EU bases, plus ~50% foreign residents and over
// 200,000 cross-border commuters from France, Belgium, and Germany.
// TIMEZONE: CET (UTC+1) / CEST (UTC+2 summer) — 1-2 hours behind
// Nairobi EAT, the standard European framing.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

